# OPEN68-STAMP — Goal: Honest listing_fresh, fail-closed hello

File: openOODA/audit/open68_stamp_goal.oot
Status: proved on the hello stamp-walk slice. Not gcc-parity. OPEN-68 not closed.
This is process, not product. Not a new backend. Not “gcc retired.”
Prior slice linked hello-check with `llvm_emit_listing_fresh_stub` (`ret i32 1`).
That OK was a nonempty `g_` listing plus a stub. Do not reopen that bar.

## 0. One-sentence goal

LLVM emit of `check_listing_fresh` is the real function. A COORD-named side ELF
prints `^OK` on `fixtures/hello.oo` twice. A stale `g_` listing or a changed
hello must not print OK. Caller cap, `sret` on 24-byte C returns, no
`declare TY @name(...)`. Two skeptic notes PASS. C emit + gcc stays product.

Active axiom: RULES 1.1 (real cause, no re-stub) and 1.6 (prove pass and
fail-closed). RULES 1.13: only `.oo` / `.oot`. RULES 1.7: new `.oo` <= 256.

## 1. Ground truth (verify before you edit)

  - Product path is C emit + gcc. Do not delete or bypass it.
  - `check_hash.oo` already walks stamps (`byte_at` 10/9). Do not gut the walk.
  - Stub lives in `llvm_emit_fn.oo` (hook) and `llvm_link_shim.oo` (`ret i32 1`).
  - `_shim.ll` `sys_exec` still calls `oo_cap_grant_sys`. `read_file` /
    `path_exists` already pass the caller cap. Keep that.
  - `llvm_emit_fntab_declares` prints `declare TY @name(...)`. Variadic
    `oo_file_stamp(%OoStr)` is ABI poison (intern / malloc abort).
  - String `!=` in `llvm_emit_binop.oo` calls `oo_str_eq` and does not invert.
    Stale stamps would look fresh. Invert NEQ.
  - Proof ELF: `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_stamp` (see scratch compiler_path.txt).
    Not tree `oodac/oodac` or `bin/ooda`.
  - Host has clang. No `llvm-link`. Do not concat past 1MiB.
  - If intern abort remains after ABI/`sret`: fail the slice. Do not re-stub.

## 2. Done means

  1. IR of `check_listing_fresh` is a real body. No `llvm_emit_listing_fresh_stub`.
  2. Side ELF `<elf> check fixtures/hello.oo` prints `^OK` and exits 0 twice.
  3. Hostile: stale `g_` listing or changed hello → no `^OK` (or rc != 0).
  4. Linked IR: no `oo_cap_grant_sys` on `sys_exec` / `read_file` / `path_exists`.
     24-byte C calls use `sret`. Known names are not `declare TY @name(...)`.
  5. `scripts/open68_stamp_smoke.oo` exists and is run. Prints PASSED and
     says C emit / gcc remains product.
  6. After builders stop: `audit/open68_stamp_sk1_claims.oot` (PV1/SEC) and
     `audit/open68_stamp_sk2_proof.oot` (PV2/MEM) both PASS on the same tip.

